Benchmark Datasets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* CounterFact (fetched on first use from
    https://rome.baulab.info/data/dsets/counterfact.json — the canonical URL
    used by the ROME implementation)
    Originally released as part of the ROME repository
    (https://github.com/kmeng01/rome) accompanying:
        Kevin Meng, David Bau, Alex Andonian, Yonatan Belinkov.
        "Locating and Editing Factual Associations in GPT."
        NeurIPS 2022.
    Distributed under the MIT License. We do NOT redistribute the JSON in
    this repository; `src/data/fact.py::_ensure_counterfact_dataset` pulls
    it from the upstream source on the first call and caches the result
    locally at `src/data/data_source/counterfact.json`.

* MedMCQA (`openlifescienceai/medmcqa`)
    Released under the Apache License 2.0:
        https://huggingface.co/datasets/openlifescienceai/medmcqa
    Pulled from the Hugging Face Hub at training/eval time;
    NOT redistributed by this repository.

* Gretel Synthetic Text-to-SQL (`gretelai/synthetic_text_to_sql`)
    Released by Gretel AI under the Apache License 2.0:
        https://huggingface.co/datasets/gretelai/synthetic_text_to_sql
    Pulled from the Hugging Face Hub at training/eval time;
    NOT redistributed by this repository.

All datasets above are used strictly for academic fine-tuning and evaluation
as intended by their creators. Please cite the original publications for each
dataset in any downstream work — see the references list of the MoLF paper.

